    "top_frame": "Tied through six innings until the seventh changed everything.",
    "what_this_means": "Machado powered early runs and Laureano broke the tie late, but the real story was the offense's conversion rate with runners in scoring position. Two of six RISP situations turned into runs. Not dominant, but enough when the bullpen cleaned up after Buehler left. Rodriguez, Morejon, Adam, and Estrada combined for 3.1 scoreless innings. The game stayed within arm's reach until the eighth exploded into a three-run lead that held. This is what stabilizing looks like from the inside: not dominant, not consistent, just executable when it matters. The Padres are 0.5 back because they're finding ways to win one-run games by finishing them late.",
